{"name":"Vinca & Vine","hex":"#45584c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vinca","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several evergreen shrubs, of the genus Vinca, including the periwinkle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vinca"},{"term":"vine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant whose stem requires support and which climbs by tendrils or twining.","Any plant the stem of which creeps along the ground."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vinca","blocks":[{"text":"Vinca is an Old World genus of flowering plants in the family Apocynaceae. The English name periwinkle is shared with the related genus Catharanthus. Some Vinca species are cultivated but have also spread invasively. Additionally, some species have medicinal uses. The most widespread species is Vinca minor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Vinca_major_closeup.jpg/330px-Vinca_major_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinca"},{"title":"Ampersand","blocks":[{"text":"The ampersand, also known as the and sign, is the logogram &, representing the conjunction \"and\". It originated as a ligature of the word et."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Et_sign.svg/330px-Et_sign.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ampersand"},{"title":"Vine","blocks":[{"text":"A vine is any plant with a growth habit of trailing or scandent stems, lianas, or runners. The word vine can also refer to such stems or runners themselves, for instance, when used in wicker work."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg/330px-%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_c